    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup heavily incentivized by stolen base upside and favorable platoon dynamics against mid-tier arms. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.33) and **Caleb Durbin** (68.14) headline our starting nine; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits significantly from a projected leadoff spot and a 14% dynamic platoon advantage, while **Caleb Durbin** exploits a high-skill matchup against an aging arm in an environment that heavily favors his aggressive baserunning profile. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (64.13) provides a strong floor, with his dynamic platoon advantage pushing him well into our \"Strong\" start tier despite facing a high-velocity threat in Roki Sasaki.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the margins involved **Pedro Ramirez** (39.24), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Kazuma Okamoto** (48.46). While **Pedro Ramirez** offers switch-hitting flexibility, his projected bottom-third lineup position suppressed his efficiency score compared to **Kazuma Okamoto**, whose middle-of-the-order placement and platoon edge against a lefty offered a safer statistical floor. We are exercising caution with **Trea Turner** (59.73) and **Kyle Schwarber** (56.90); despite their elite pedigree, the wind-in conditions at their respective venues introduced enough volatility to temper their output expectations, though their status as focal points in the lineup keeps them locked in for game cap allocation.\n\nManaging risk remains critical today, as nine of our eleven starters rely on pending lineup confirmations. Specifically, the matchups for **Gary Sanchez** against Roki Sasaki and **Jacob Gonzalez** against Phillips are volatile; should their actual batting orders drop significantly, their already marginal scores could dip below our efficiency threshold. We remain without production from **Yordan Alvarez** and **Junior Caminero** due to scheduled off-days, placing a premium on the stolen base output expected from **Caleb Durbin**, **Trea Turner**, and **Christian Yelich** to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 standings.",
